<h2 class="h3" style="margin:0 0 var(--space-2)">Use it in your prototype</h2>
<p class="muted" style="margin:0 0 var(--space-3)">Paste these lines into the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> of your HTML file, tokens first. Then use the classes on this page, adding a type class to each component, e.g. <code>&lt;button class="body pdg-btn pdg-btn--primary"&gt;Start workout&lt;/button&gt;</code>.</p>
<pre style="margin:0;padding:var(--space-4);background:var(--surface);border:var(--border-width) solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-3);overflow-x:auto;font:13px/20px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;color:var(--text)">&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:opsz,wght@9..40,400..700&amp;display=swap"&gt;
&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://phoebeyudesign.github.io/ProductDesignerGym/tokens.css"&gt;
&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://phoebeyudesign.github.io/ProductDesignerGym/components/bundle.css"&gt;</pre>
</div>
<div class="brandbook body" style="margin-top:var(--space-6)"><p>A dark, neon-lit system for Product Designer Gym: interfaces that feel like a training floor for design skills — a dark canvas, one electric-blue action colour, and plain, confident DM Sans type.</p>
<h2>Brand</h2>
<ul>
<li>Write the name as <strong>Product Designer Gym</strong> — three words, title case, never abbreviated in UI copy.</li>
<li>The logo is a photographed neon sign: a flexed-arm icon inside a design-tool selection frame (corner handles), a sparkle and a cursor, over the stacked wordmark. Use <code>product-designer-gym-neon.png</code> from <strong>Logos</strong> as a hero or brand image on <code>background</code>; it carries its own brick-wall backdrop, so never place it on a light ground or crop the sign's glow tightly.</li>
<li>The sign's violet sparkle, pink frame and orange cursor belong to the logo image only. They are <strong>not</strong> UI colours: interfaces use the tokens below.</li>
<li>No vector mark has been supplied, so there is no small-size logo or favicon yet. Do not redraw the sign; set the name in <code>h4</code> / <code>text</code> where a compact mark is needed.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Colour</h2>
<p>The system has one theme, <strong>Dark</strong>.</p>
<ul>
<li>Paint the app canvas <code>background</code>; cards, modals and input fields <code>surface</code>.</li>
<li>Set headings and body copy in <code>text</code>; secondary text, hints and descriptions in <code>text-muted</code>.</li>
<li>Use <code>primary</code> for primary actions, links and active elements, and <code>primary-hover</code> only for their hover state — it is not a second brand colour.</li>
<li>Label any <code>primary</code>, <code>primary-hover</code> or <code>error</code> fill with <code>on-primary</code> (the dark canvas colour). White on <code>primary</code> is 1.9:1 and fails.</li>
<li>Use <code>success</code> for successful outcomes, <code>warning</code> for caution and <code>error</code> for errors or destructive actions. Never signal status through colour alone: pair it with an icon and a word (see <strong>StatusBadge</strong>).</li>
<li>Use <code>border</code> for dividers, outlines and input borders. It measures 2.6:1 on <code>background</code> and 2.3:1 on <code>surface</code>, under the 3:1 recommended for control boundaries — rely on the field's <code>surface</code> fill and its label as well as the outline, and use the <code>primary</code> focus ring to mark the active field.</li>
<li>Check contrast for each actual pairing; target WCAG AA — 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text and for meaningful graphics and control boundaries.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Typography</h2>
<ul>
<li>Set everything in DM Sans (<code>--font-sans</code>). It is a hosted Google Font: load it in the project before applying these tokens, e.g. <code>https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:opsz,wght@9..40,400..700&amp;display=swap</code>.</li>
<li>Headings: <code>h1</code> 40/48 bold for page titles (one per page; about 32px on small screens), <code>h2</code> 32/40 bold for sections, <code>h3</code> 24/32 semibold for subsections, <code>h4</code> 20/28 semibold for card and component titles. Keep them in descending order.</li>
<li>Text: <code>body</code> 16/24 for primary content, <code>caption</code> 14/20 for supporting information, <code>small</code> 12/16 for secondary labels and timestamps.</li>
<li>Reserve <code>tiny</code> (10/12, medium) for nonessential decorative metadata; keep anything essential at 12px or larger.</li>
<li>Apply type through the type-style classes (<code>class="body"</code>, <code>caption</code>, <code>h4</code>, <code>small</code>…), never by hard-coding a font size. Components set only a weight on top of them (labels and badges at 600).</li>
</ul>
<h2>Spacing and layout</h2>
<ul>
<li>Use only the spacing scale <code>space-1</code> (4px) to <code>space-7</code> (48px) — no arbitrary numbers.</li>
<li>Default gaps are <code>space-4</code> (16px), card padding is <code>space-5</code> (24px), and major sections sit <code>space-7</code> (48px) apart. Inputs pad at <code>space-3</code>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Radii</h2>
<ul>
<li>Buttons and inputs <code>radius-2</code> (8px); cards and dropdowns <code>radius-3</code> (12px); larger panels <code>radius-4</code> (16px); badges and small controls <code>radius-1</code> (4px).</li>
<li>Use <code>radius-none</code> (0) for full-bleed images and tables that run edge to edge, and <code>radius-full</code> (9999px) for pills and circles.</li>
<li>Keep radii consistent between related components. Use <code>radius-5</code> and <code>radius-full</code> selectively, for hero, feature and pill shapes.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Borders</h2>
<ul>
<li>Draw every outline and divider at <code>border-width</code> (1px) and every focus outline at <code>focus-ring-width</code> (2px) — never a literal pixel width.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Interaction</h2>
<ul>
<li>One visually dominant primary button per screen or task area; everything else is secondary or ghost.</li>
<li>Every interactive element shows a visible keyboard focus state: a solid <code>focus-ring-width</code> <code>primary</code> ring with a 2px offset (8.8:1 on <code>background</code>, 7.8:1 on <code>surface</code>).</li>
<li>Destructive actions use <code>error</code> and say what they destroy ("Delete workout").</li>
</ul>
<h2>Iconography</h2>
<p>No icon set has been supplied. The logo's motifs — the selection frame with corner handles, the sparkle and the cursor — are the brand's visual language; when an icon set is chosen, prefer a single-weight outline style that matches the neon tubing, and always pair status icons with a word.</p>
<h2>Components</h2>
<p>The component styles live in <code>components/bundle.css</code> as plain CSS classes (prefix <code>pdg-</code>); there is no JavaScript bundle. The spec names actions, inputs, cards and status colours, so the system includes <strong>Button</strong>, <strong>Input</strong>, <strong>Card</strong> and <strong>StatusBadge</strong> built strictly from these tokens.</p></div>
</section>
<section id="colour"><h2 class="h2">Colour</h2><p class="lede">One dark theme. Contrast ratios are measured against <code>background</code> and <code>surface</code>.</p><div class="swatches"><article class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background:var(--primary)"></div>
<div class="sw-meta"><div class="sw-head"><span class="sw-name">primary</span><span class="sw-val">#00BFFF</span></div>
<p class="sw-usage caption">Primary actions, links and active elements. As text: 8.8:1 on <code>background</code>, 7.8:1 on <code>surface</code>. As a fill, label it with <code>on-primary</code>, never white (white on primary is 1.9:1). Also the keyboard focus ring.</p>
<p class="sw-ratio small">8.8:1 on background · 7.8:1 on surface</p></div></article><article class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background:var(--primary-hover)"></div>
<div class="sw-meta"><div class="sw-head"><span class="sw-name">primary-hover</span><span class="sw-val">#33CCFF</span></div>
<p class="sw-usage caption">Hover state of anything painted in <code>primary</code> — never a second primary colour.</p>
<p class="sw-ratio small">9.9:1 on background · 8.8:1 on surface</p></div></article><article class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background:var(--on-primary)"></div>
<div class="sw-meta"><div class="sw-head"><span class="sw-name">on-primary</span><span class="sw-val">#111318 · {background}</span></div>
<p class="sw-usage caption">Labels and icons on <code>primary</code> / <code>primary-hover</code> fills (8.8:1 / 9.9:1). Added alongside the spec: the spec gives no text colour for primary fills.</p>
<p class="sw-ratio small">1.0:1 on background · 1.1:1 on surface</p></div></article><article class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background:var(--background)"></div>
<div class="sw-meta"><div class="sw-head"><span class="sw-name">background</span><span class="sw-val">#111318</span></div>
<p class="sw-usage caption">The main app canvas.</p>
<p class="sw-ratio small">1.0:1 on background · 1.1:1 on surface</p></div></article><article class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background:var(--surface)"></div>
<div class="sw-meta"><div class="sw-head"><span class="sw-name">surface</span><span class="sw-val">#1B1F2A</span></div>
<p class="sw-usage caption">Cards, modals and input backgrounds, on top of <code>background</code>.</p>
<p class="sw-ratio small">1.1:1 on background · 1.0:1 on surface</p></div></article><article class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background:var(--text)"></div>
<div class="sw-meta"><div class="sw-head"><span class="sw-name">text</span><span class="sw-val">#F5F5F5</span></div>
<p class="sw-usage caption">Headings and primary body text on <code>background</code> (17:1) and <code>surface</code> (15.1:1).</p>
<p class="sw-ratio small">17.0:1 on background · 15.1:1 on surface</p></div></article><article class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background:var(--text-muted)"></div>
<div class="sw-meta"><div class="sw-head"><span class="sw-name">text-muted</span><span class="sw-val">#C4CAD4</span></div>
<p class="sw-usage caption">Secondary text, hints and descriptions on <code>background</code> (11.3:1) and <code>surface</code> (10:1).</p>
<p class="sw-ratio small">11.3:1 on background · 10.0:1 on surface</p></div></article><article class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background:var(--border)"></div>
<div class="sw-meta"><div class="sw-head"><span class="sw-name">border</span><span class="sw-val">#515867</span></div>
<p class="sw-usage caption">Dividers, outlines and input borders. Contrast flag: 2.6:1 on <code>background</code>, 2.3:1 on <code>surface</code> — below the 3:1 the spec asks of control boundaries, so fine for decorative dividers; an input relying on this outline alone to be found does not meet it.</p>
<p class="sw-ratio small">2.6:1 on background · 2.3:1 on surface</p></div></article><article class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background:var(--success)"></div>
<div class="sw-meta"><div class="sw-head"><span class="sw-name">success</span><span class="sw-val">#00E676</span></div>
<p class="sw-usage caption">Successful outcomes. Always paired with an icon or word. As text: 11.1:1 on <code>background</code>, 9.9:1 on <code>surface</code>.</p>
<p class="sw-ratio small">11.1:1 on background · 9.9:1 on surface</p></div></article><article class="swatch"><div class="chip" style="background:var(--warning)"></div>
<div class="sw-meta"><div class="sw-head"><span class="sw-name">warning</span><span class="sw-val">#FFD166</span></div>
<p class="sw-usage caption">Caution. Always paired with an icon or word. As text: 12.9:1 on <code>background</code>, 11.4:1 on <code>surface</code>.</p>
